🔹 What is Next.js and why use it?
Next.js is a React framework for building server-side rendered (SSR) and statically generated (SSG) applications.
Better SEO due to SSR
Built-in API routes (no need for separate backend for small apps)
Image optimization (next/image)
Automatic code splitting and file-based routing
Supports TypeScript, Tailwind, middleware, and app route

🔹What are the different rendering methods in Next.js
SSR (Server-Side Rendering):
Page is rendered on every request (getServerSideProps).
SSG (Static Site Generation):
Page is pre-rendered at build time (getStaticProps).
ISR (Incremental Static Regeneration):
Static pages can be updated after build using revalidation.
CSR (Client-Side Rendering):
Data fetched with useEffect or SWR on client side.

🔹Difference between getStaticProps, getServerSideProps, and getStaticPaths?
getStaticProps: Fetch data at build time → used for static generation.
getServerSideProps: Fetch data on each request → used for dynamic pages.
getStaticPaths: Used with dynamic routes ([id].js) to pre-render specific paths at build time.

🔹How do you optimize performance in Next.js?
Use code splitting & dynamic imports (next/dynamic).
Use Image optimization.
Use ISR for fresh content without overloading the server.
Cache responses using SWR or React Query.
Use Middleware for lightweight auth checks.